WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.070
July 2020.

2
00:00:02.120 --> 00:00:05.150
Famous accounts on Twitter, now called X,

3
00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:09.390
all start posting the same
thing: a bitcoin scam.

4
00:00:09.440 --> 00:00:15.170
130 accounts were targeted:
politicians, celebrities and businesses.

5
00:00:15.220 --> 00:00:17.490
These were well-protected accounts.

6
00:00:17.540 --> 00:00:21.010
So how did attackers take
control of so many at once?

7
00:00:21.060 --> 00:00:22.970
Did they find a bug in the code?

8
00:00:23.020 --> 00:00:25.650
Guess every password, one by one?

9
00:00:25.700 --> 00:00:27.850
Or did they hack something else?

10
00:00:27.900 --> 00:00:30.730
In this mission, you'll
meet social engineering:

11
00:00:30.780 --> 00:00:33.510
manipulating people, not machines.

12
00:00:33.560 --> 00:00:39.130
You'll see how phishing uses fake messages
and fake websites to steal login details.

13
00:00:39.180 --> 00:00:43.190
And you'll learn how training and
simple checks can protect people.

14
00:00:43.240 --> 00:00:46.560
Your mission: find out what
the hackers really hacked.
